"object": {
"desc": "A magnetised T letterform ringed by four rotating lines of text, with chrome discs descending and renewing below. With a switchable background and a grid floor, this is the canonical object from which every work begins.",
"frag": "Four rows of text revolve without pause, each row set against the next so that it cannot be read to its end. When it was first observed it was not new. The lattice around it had already been laid to its shape, and where its shadow fell the ground was weathered. Removal was attempted once. The procedure was completed, the members were carried out, the site was surveyed. On the following week's map the same shape appeared at a different scale.",
"log": "It was first observed. It was not new.",
"name": "Object",
"phase": "PHASE 1 · THE FIRST T"
},
"preservation-hall": {
"desc": "The preservation hall of THE INDIVIDUAL, where the two awoke. Some hundred and sixty days after waking; the two are absent. Seventy-two pods stand on twelve rising tiers, and two of them are open. On the wall terminal the measurement record runs; only its second line rewrites itself every 0.78 seconds, and it is always out of tolerance. A root comes out of the wall and passes through the ceiling, and beyond the open door there is a forest. Three places to stand: beside a pod, before the terminal, and at the door. Only the head turns. Touch a thing and it returns its record of observation.",
"frag": "The pods are six across and twelve deep. Seventy-two. Two are open; their lids have withdrawn on the axis at the pillow end and stand there, and do not return. Seventy remain closed, and beneath the clouded lids a thin pink layer can be seen as far as its colour, and no farther. One part of the wall is smoother than the rest, and there the measurement record runs. The base is 0.78. The tolerance is 0.01 either way. Only the second line rewrites itself with each pulse, and it is always outside the tolerance. At the bottom: send. Beneath it: apply. Everything sent was accepted; nothing was received. A root comes out of the wall and passes through the ceiling. It did not break in. It is part of the surface. The door has been unlocked from the first day and open since the twenty-ninth, and twenty paces out the root road begins. In the corner of the forecourt lie six shells that fit no one, and a small heap of cut hair. The pile of a hundred packets ran out three days ago.",
"log": "Every submission was accepted. None was received.",
"name": "The Preservation Hall",
"phase": "PHASE UNRESOLVED · THE INDIVIDUAL"
},
"residual-index-53": {
"desc": "The first novel of the series, bound as if by a later compiler: corporate audit records, house organs, three schools of exegesis, and the reports of a verifier circuiting a star system. ASSET 17, The Vacant Seat, comes from chapter eleven. Complete text.",
"frag": "Stand still in the middle of the corridor and the sound of the building arrives as one sound. Conveyors, valves, lifts, ventilation. The sources are several hundred and separate, but the pulse coincides exactly, so the ear cannot part them. One receives the impression of a single vast device breathing slowly. Impressions are not matters for audit, and the observation ends here.",
"log": "The standard was enforced. Its origin was not on file.",
"name": "Residual Index 53",
"phase": "PHASE −2 · ANTHROPOCENTRIC EXPANSION"
},
"sanctum": {
"desc": "A sanctum in a subterranean cavern. A fusion core and a brain core, with heavy power trunks driven into the rock wall, enclosed by a dome of stone and stalactites. Era switches the grade between Y2K and the current one; Next view cycles the viewpoints. Absorbs the former Vault v4.",
"frag": "The cavern was not excavated. A body of rock, selected for the convenience of cooling, became the vessel as it stood. The walls were not dressed, and the dripstone was left where it hung. Removal was not included in the schedule of works, nor was any reason for its exclusion sought. The trunks reach deep into their mouths in the rock, and the plan of the districts beyond them is held as a separate volume. That volume is at present stored within this cavern.",
"log": "Purpose expired. Maintenance continued.",
"name": "Sanctum v5",
"phase": "PHASE 5 · RESIDUAL WORLD"
},
"sigil-fusion": {
"desc": "The only work set on white. The artwork itself uses no raster; SVG and arithmetic alone keep the beat. Three rings of circling text enclose the cortex while wafers descend below, shrinking as they fall. The artwork itself uses no WebGL.",
"frag": "Three rings revolve at differing rates, tuned so as to hold no period in common. By calculation there exists no instant at which they coincide. No altar was required. Neither offering, nor a place to kneel, nor any who recite. What was required was a ratio. For this reason the rite does not end. The habit of calling that which does not end a faith had, by this time, fallen out of use.",
"log": "Ascension no longer required belief.",
"name": "Sigil Fusion v5",
"phase": "PHASE 3 · TRANSCENSION"
},
